---
// The extension's policy comes from PRIVACY.md in the repo, so the store, GitHub and this page
// always say the same thing. The section about this website is added here.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { Content } from '../../../PRIVACY.md';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy – Canvas Course Downloader"
  description="What the extension and this website collect: nothing about you leaves your browser except requests to your own Canvas. Every permission and why it's needed."
  ogTitle="Privacy policy"
  current="/privacy/"
>
  <section class="wrap narrow page-head">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      What the extension and this website do with your data. In short: nothing about you or your
      courses leaves your browser, apart from the requests to your own Canvas.
    </p>
  </section>
  <article class="wrap narrow prose doc">
    <Content />
    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      This website sets no cookies. It counts visits with Umami, open-source analytics that runs on
      our own server in Germany: it stores no IP addresses and can't tell who you are, nothing is
      shared with anyone, and it skips browsers that send Do Not Track. The server keeps short
      technical logs, such as IP addresses, for security.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
